<title>FRANCE: Tunisia buys 125,000 tonnes wheat.</title>
<headline>Tunisia buys 125,000 tonnes wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia on Wednesday bought 125,000 tonnes of Canadian, U.S. or European wheat for shipment between July and September at prices which include $176.50 per tonne with freight for July, grain traders said.  </p>
<p>Tunisian traders put the price range at $173.42 to $176.5 C&amp;F for five lots of 25,000 tonnes each.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
